==Russian==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*bur'a}}, akin to Bulgarian {{m|bg|буря}}, Slovene {{m|sl|burja}}, Polish {{m|pl|burza}},  Serbo-Croatian {{m|sh|бура}}/{{m|sh|bura}}, Slovak {{m|sk|búrka||tempest}} and {{m|sk|búrať||to crush}}. Non-Slavic cognates include Old Norse {{m|non|byrr||fair wind}}, Latin {{m|la|furo||I rage, rave}}, Sanskrit {{m|sa|भुरति||stir, palpitate}}. Compare also {{cog|tr|bora||squall}}.

